Minimum Absolute Difference in Sliding Submatrix (LeetCode 3567)
Problem Overview
You are given a matrix and a size k. For every k x k submatrix, you must find the minimum absolute difference between any two distinct values.
Key Idea
Instead of comparing all pairs, we sort the distinct values. The minimum absolute difference will always be between adjacent elements in sorted order.
Methodology
1. Slide a k x k window over the matrix.
2. Extract all elements inside the submatrix.
3. Remove duplicates using a set.
4. Sort the values.
5. Compute minimum difference between adjacent elements.
6. If only one unique value exists, return 0.
Example
Grid: [[1, -2, 3], [2, 3, 5]], k = 2

Submatrix 1: [1, -2, 2, 3] -> Sorted: [-2,1,2,3] -> Min diff = 1
Submatrix 2: [-2, 3, 3, 5] -> Unique: [-2,3,5] -> Min diff = 2
Why It Works
Sorting ensures that the closest numbers are adjacent. This reduces complexity compared to checking all pairs.
Time Complexity
O((m-k+1)*(n-k+1) * k^2 log k)
Space Complexity
O(k^2)
